# Design system

Use **Bronze Spice** (`spice-*`) for brand/accent color and **neutral** semantic tokens for layout, text, and surfaces. Do not use cyan, blue, or unrelated accent colors unless the user asks.

## Spice scale (Tailwind: `spice-50` … `spice-950`)

| Token | Hex |
|-------|-----|
| 50 | `#FFF1E6` |
| 100 | `#FFE2CC` |
| 200 | `#FEC59A` |
| 300 | `#FEA867` |
| 400 | `#FE8C34` |
| 500 | `#FE6F01` |
| 600 | `#CB5901` |
| 700 | `#984201` |
| 800 | `#652C01` |
| 900 | `#331600` |
| 950 | `#240F00` |

## Semantic tokens (prefer these in components)

- `text-accent` / `bg-accent` — primary brand (`spice-500`, `#FE6F01`)
- `text-accent-highlight` — emphasized words (`spice-400`, `#FE8C34`)
- `text-accent-muted` — darker accent (`spice-700`)
- `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `bg-background`, `bg-surface`, `border-border` — neutrals (theme-aware light/dark)

## Usage

- Highlights and secondary emphasis: `text-accent-highlight` or `spice-400`, not `text-cyan-*`.
- Gradients and glows: `spice-400` / `spice-500` / `spice-600`, not blue or red Tailwind defaults.
- Backgrounds and body text: neutral semantic tokens, not raw slate/blue grays.

Defined in `src/index.css` `@theme` and `.dark` overrides.
